sa yogī paramo mataḥ\"}]},{\"section\":\"synonyms\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.synonyms\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"books.Synonyms\",\"title\":\"synonyms\",\"id\":1965,\"bb\":1737,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/6/32/b1737/\",\"shadow_value\":\"ātma – with his self; aupamyena – by comparison; sarvatra – everywhere; samam – equally; paśyati – sees; yaḥ – he who; arjuna – O Arjuna; sukham – happiness; vā – or; yadi – if; vā – or; duḥkham – distress; saḥ – such; yogī – a transcendentalist; paramaḥ – perfect; mataḥ – is considered.\",\"word_for_word_value\":[{\"word\":\"ātma\",\"translation\":\"with his self\"},{\"word\":\"aupamyena\",\"translation\":\"by comparison\"},{\"word\":\"sarvatra\",\"translation\":\"everywhere\"},{\"word\":\"samam\",\"translation\":\"equally\"},{\"word\":\"paśyati\",\"translation\":\"sees\"},{\"word\":\"yaḥ\",\"translation\":\"he who\"},{\"word\":\"arjuna\",\"translation\":\"O Arjuna\"},{\"word\":\"sukham\",\"translation\":\"happiness\"},{\"word\":\"vā\",\"translation\":\"or\"},{\"word\":\"yadi\",\"translation\":\"if\"},{\"word\":\"vā\",\"translation\":\"or\"},{\"word\":\"duḥkham\",\"translation\":\"distress\"},{\"word\":\"saḥ\",\"translation\":\"such\"},{\"word\":\"yogī\",\"translation\":\"a transcendentalist\"},{\"word\":\"paramaḥ\",\"translation\":\"perfect\"},{\"word\":\"mataḥ\",\"translation\":\"is considered\"}]}]},{\"section\":\"translation\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.translation\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"translation\",\"id\":1966,\"bb\":1738,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/6/32/b1738/\",\"body_value\":\"He is a perfect yogī who, by comparison to his own self, sees the true equality of all beings, in both their happiness and their distress, O Arjuna!\"}]},{\"section\":\"purport\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.purport\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":1967,\"bb\":1739,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/6/32/b1739/\",\"body_value\":\"$25\"}]}],\"short_title\":\"B